          "id": "SP_TEDANIA_CHARCOTI_TOPSENT_1907",
          "name": "Tedania charcoti Topsent, 1907",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Tedania",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "(Figure 8 f) Restricted synonymy: Tedania charcoti Topsent, 1907. Material examined: 1 specimen collected in station 4 (SOI; 60 ° 55 ' S, 44 ° 04 ' W; 256 m; 2 / 3 / 2014; MACN-In 44398). Description: Massive sponge, red / brownish (Figure 8 f). Surface uneven and porous. Spicules are styles 380 – 530 µm by 20 µm, anisotornotes of 220 – 300 µm by 5 µm and onychaetes of 105 – 285 µm. Remarks: This is a common species, widely distributed in Antarctic and sub Antarctic waters (e. g. Desqueyroux-Faúndez 1989; Ríos et al. 2004; Goodwin et al. 2019; Schejter et al. 2006, Bertolino et al. 2007; Fernández et al. 2021). See Ríos (2006) for a complete description. It was previously recorded from the SOI by Burton (1940).",
