          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Tedania",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "(Figure 8 b – e) Restricted synonymy: Oceanapia kirkpatricki Hentschel, 1914, Tedania (Tedaniopsis) actiniiformis Ridley & Dendy, 1886. Material examined: 1 specimen collected at station 1 (SOI; 60 ° 28 ' S, 46 ° 29 ' W; 139 m; 19 / 2 / 2014; MACN-In 44399; IEO-CSIC Col.). Description: Massive sponge, soft, beige in colour, cavernous, with abundant mucus. Spicules are large styles of 600 – 710 µm by 25 – 30 µm, anisotornotes of 350 – 430 µm by 10 µm, onychaetes I of 290 – 730 µm and onychaetes I of ~ 90 µm (Figure 8 b – e). Remarks: This species has been previously reported from Antarctic and subantarctic waters by Burton (1932, 1934, 1938), Hentschel (1914), and in Patagonia (Burton 1940; Bertolino et al. 2007). This is the first record for the SOI.",
